in current django where to put

Where to put Oracle database connection code in a current Django project?
(2025–2026 best practices)

Here are the most common and recommended places depending on how and when you want to use the Oracle connection:
#	Where to put the code	When to use it	Pros	Cons / Limitations	Recommended for
1	settings.py → DATABASES configuration	Normal Django ORM usage	Cleanest, standard Django way	Only for Django models / ORM	★★★★★ Most projects
2	Custom database backend (inherits from oracledb)	Special connection pooling / tweaks	Full control over connection	Quite complex to implement	Advanced cases
3	Utility module (e.g. utils/db.py or core/db.py)	Raw SQL queries, scripts, management commands	Simple, reusable, no ORM needed	You manage connections yourself	Your current case (probably best)
4	Django management command	Periodic jobs, one-time data migrations	Clean separation	Not suitable for views/services	Batch processing
5	Celery task / Background task	Long running / async processing	Doesn't block web requests	Requires Celery setup	Heavy processing
6	Custom context processor / middleware	Very rare – per request connection	—	Very bad practice (connection per request)	Almost never
Most Recommended for Your Situation (raw select + insert)
Bash

your_project/
